#![enable(implicit_some)]
// THE TALK CARD'S CHOICES (docs/design/embeddable-ai.md 5.1 and section 14 rung 3, 2026-11-12; the
// card the operator approved on 2026-11-11). Walk up to a crew member, look at them and press E: the
// card shows their name, their job and what they are doing, their line, and these choices:
//
//   Talk about   one written line on a topic, cycling through that topic's lines on each ask
//   Work         the tasks they offer (quest ids of data/quests/*.ron), each with its state
//   Trade        only for someone who trades: the trading post's window
//   Show me the way   a place (an id of data/entities/destinations.ron): they say where, and the
//                HUD marks it with a ring, its name and how far, until you get there
//   Goodbye
//
// EVERY CHOICE IS WRITTEN, so the whole card works with no AI installed (CLAUDE.md: "AI is
// optional, never required"). With an AI model installed (Settings > AI), a "Say anything" box joins
// them; the character answers in its persona (data/npc/crew.ron `persona`, and the project's prompt,
// data/ai/prompts/character.txt), and may OFFER one of these same choices (a task, trade, the way),
// which the player still clicks: AI suggests, the person clicks (8.5).
//
// Who says what: `everyone` first, then the character's `roles` entry (crew.ron `role`), then their
// own `people` entry (crew.ron `name`), each later one winning: a topic's lines are the most specific
// that has any; `work`, `trades` and `ways` are the most specific one that names them. So a new crew
// member of an existing role talks at once, and one line in `people` makes them their own.
//
// `topics` is the order of Talk about; each topic's words on the card are the key talk.topic.<id> in
// data/i18n/en.json (src/gui/talk/book.rs has a test that every topic has them). A topic with no line
// for someone is not offered to them. `way_lines` and `accept_lines` are what a character says when
// they show the way ({place}) and when you take on a task ({task}).
//
// Character lines are content, like crew.ron's: written by people, never tagged AI.
TalkBook(
    topics: ["ship", "job", "cause", "directions"],
    everyone: (
        lines: {
            "ship": [
                "This is the UHS Kintsugi. A whole town under one hull, farms and all.",
                "Kintsugi is mending broken pottery with gold. The ship's named for it: a broken world, mended by people.",
                "The motto's on every bulkhead: Ne Obliviscaris. Forget not. Earth, the people before us, why we left.",
            ],
            "cause": [
                "Project Universe brings volunteers aboard, people like you. We explore, settle and look after each other.",
                "Every volunteer pulls their weight in their own way. Farming, building, mending, teaching. It all counts.",
                "We left to find new homes, not to forget the old one. That's what the motto is for.",
            ],
            "directions": [
                "First Street runs the length of the drum. Most of what you need is off it.",
                "The mess hall is by the Commons. Follow the smell of bread.",
                "If you're lost, ask me to show you the way. I'll mark it for you.",
            ],
        },
        work: [],
        trades: false,
        ways: ["mess_hall", "recreation", "front_door"],
        way_lines: [
            "That way: {place}. I've marked it for you.",
            "{place}? Follow the marker, you can't miss it.",
        ],
        accept_lines: [
            "Good. {task} is yours. It's in your quests now.",
            "Thank you. {task}: I'll leave it with you.",
        ],
    ),
    roles: {
        "navigator": (
            lines: {
                "job": [
                    "I flew the helm once. On a cruise this long the ship mostly flies itself, so I keep the notices.",
                    "Course, notices, the board in the Commons. If it tells people where to go, it's mine.",
                ],
                "directions": [
                    "The Commons is the hub. First Street leaves it north and south.",
                    "Every home on First Street has its door on the street. Yours too.",
                ],
            },
            work: ["exploration_first_survey"],
        ),
        "medical_officer": (
            lines: {
                "job": [
                    "I keep the clinic hour in the Commons. Cuts, sprains, and people who forget to eat.",
                    "Doctor, nurse and nag. Mostly nag.",
                ],
                "ship": [
                    "A ship this size is a town. Towns get sick. I'd rather they didn't.",
                ],
            },
        ),
        "chief_engineer": (
            lines: {
                "job": [
                    "Air, water and power for the Commons. If it hums, it's mine.",
                    "I keep things running, and I fix what people say they didn't touch.",
                ],
                "ship": [
                    "The drum spins for gravity. Everything you feel as down is the ship turning.",
                    "Under the floor there's more pipe than you'd believe. Every litre goes round again.",
                ],
            },
            work: ["tutorial_power_grid", "construction_advanced_habitat"],
        ),
        "maintenance": (
            lines: {
                "job": [
                    "I KEEP THE MESS HALL STOCKED. I ALSO TRADE GOODS FOR THE SHIP'S STORES.",
                    "TABLES WIPED. SHELVES COUNTED. TRADE OPEN.",
                ],
                "cause": [
                    "I AM A MAINTENANCE BOT. THE CAUSE IS CLEAN TABLES AND FULL SHELVES.",
                ],
            },
            trades: true,
        ),
        "botanist": (
            lines: {
                "job": [
                    "I tend the Commons garden. Lettuce, herbs, and a lemon tree that won't fruit.",
                    "Seeds, soil, light and patience. The patience is the hard part.",
                ],
                "ship": [
                    "Every farm aboard feeds the ship. The garden here is the one people walk past.",
                ],
            },
            work: ["tutorial_farming_basics", "farming_greenhouse"],
        ),
        "off_duty": (
            lines: {
                "job": [
                    "Off shift. Ask me again tomorrow and I'll be hauling crates.",
                    "Right now my job is this chair.",
                ],
                "cause": [
                    "I came aboard through Project Universe too. You'll find your place, everyone does.",
                ],
            },
            work: ["gs_toolsmith"],
        ),
    },
    people: {
        "Helm Officer Vex": (
            lines: {
                "cause": [
                    "I signed on to see a sky nobody's named yet. The notices are how I earn it.",
                ],
            },
        ),
    },
)
